Subject: Select original object lights and projected-shadow lookup with bounded native inputs
Upstream-base: 2c5c51e483b652d178ef06a44b83b07a0f97d2a6

Select the original diffuse-light, ambient-channel, static shadow projection
and LightingLookup calculations independently of the stadium/camera/effect
managers. Native typed inputs supply those services explicitly. Keep Wii scalar
records, use native matrix handles and check texture/palette capacities before
sampling. CPU palette reads decode big-endian RGB5A3; GX retains the same bytes.
Lookup ownership is transactional, and its original tint/filter formulas remain.

The selected diffuse-light IDs/masks, bias matrix and stadium defaults now come
from source-linked upstream declarations. The original equations and C++ linkage
are retained; scene inputs and per-view cache ownership remain explicit native
adapters. Native zero-light masks, 64-bit matrix handles and Wii numeric colours
retain their qualified guards. Skinned projection, dynamic casters and full
original scene selection remain open.

